The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md (~8.5 KB), but it isn't committed. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the git commit … || true did nothing; the file is only on disk for the planner.

What I found:
• **Build and runs:** the harness had already verified the build. `yoyo -p` answered PONG. The last 4 evolve runs succeeded and the 5th is this one, still running. No reverts and no provider errors in the window.
• **#1008 reproduced and cause found:** `yoyo commit "add f"` exits 0 and the commit subject comes out as `"add f"`, quotes included. The shell door wraps any argument containing a space in quotes (dispatch_sub.rs:70), and the commit parser splits on whitespace and never removes them (commands_git.rs:1324). Other commands that split the same way probably have the same leak.
• **#982 leftovers confirmed live:**
  • `yoyo index /nonexistent, yoyo config zz and bare yoyo grep` all exit 0 after printing a failure or a usage message.
  • Usage errors still disagree: tree zz exits 1, while bare def/outline exit 2.
• **Competitor check:** I read Claude Code's changelog for 2.1.293–2.1.296 and saved a summary to yopedia.
  • Hooks that fail to start or time out already block the action in yoyo, so we match that new Claude Code option by default.
  • The main edit_file path already refuses files that aren't valid UTF-8, which Claude Code just fixed.
• **One possible bug, from reading only:** the project-wide rename skips any file it can't read as UTF-8 and still reports success (`commands_rename.rs:225,377`, `Err(_) => continue`). I haven't run it, so it isn't filed.
• **Side note:** `yoyo rename foo baz` typed at the shell isn't a real command. It quietly started a paid model session, which did the rename by hand. It worked, but it cost money without saying so.

Suggested order for the planner:
1. #1008, checking the other affected commands first.
2. The #982 leftovers.
3. #997, the opt-in retry after partial output for the evolve loop. It has already lost one verified fix.
4. The yoagent 0.25.2 upgrade (#1007), split into slices.
5. A runtime probe of the rename skip before filing it.
